# INSTALLATION

## Intented audience

This manual is intented to future "admins" of an Adelphos instance and also
to future developers; it is not intended to be read by end users who should
look at the docs/user folder instead.

## Prerequisites.

Adelphos is a project written in Python and for now it has been tested on
two ubuntu systems without any problem. It should run on any Linux system,
though. I have tried it in a Ubuntu VM in Windows and it worked, however I
have not yet tried to not tried to run it on WSL on Linux

It is handled by uv, a python package manager, so you should install it
first. Instructions to install it are found here.

https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/

# Sync the packages

After uv has been installed you can sync the packages, please type

> uv sync

in the root of the project and the package manager will download all the
relevant packages.

# Test the installation

After installing the packages it is a good idea to test the installation.
First of all you should activate the virtual environment, to do so type

. ./.venv/bin/activate

The shell prompt will reflect the change. After this you can type

pytest 

And all the tests (currently 125, but their number grows...) will be run
(total extimated time 90 seconds).

They should run all OK. In some cases, especially with system with a high
load, a test might fail, but this is a false positive, re-run it with an
idle machine and it should go.

If all goes well you are now ready to create an adelphos instance.

